  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One pipeline, several entrances",
      "items": [
        "Slash/CLI/API calls, stored schedules and the workflow meta-tool resolve enabled shared/personal recipe definitions. Personal same-id files override shared files.",
        "Required tools must be available in the selected mode and execution surface. Optional unavailable tools are skipped; admission and execution recheck the recipe."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Ordered work and source identity",
      "items": [
        "The recipe chooses tools; optional parameter filling, conditions, validation and final summaries can call an LLM. Explicit tools still run when provider-native helper tools are disabled.",
        "for_each loops retain named validated_output_var outputs. search_output_var isolates provider URL lists; source arguments and stash:// references accompany results for follow-up. Authored Stash filenames stay intact and on_conflict controls repeat saves."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Truthful completion",
      "items": [
        "Workflow component calls stay foreground. A queued background receipt is rejected rather than reported as successful workflow work. Long external operations retain their task IDs and uncertain outcomes.",
        "Required failures abort unless explicitly continued; optional work may degrade the result. Cancellation returns partial evidence. Success and failure include step results, tools, mode, timing and usage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Email and scheduled tasks",
      "items": [
        "jarvis_email_inbox is a normal scheduled recipe whose in-process tool polls Gmail, verifies approved-sender requests and attachments, runs restricted orchestration and sends a threaded sender-only reply.",
        "Notification-only schedule edits keep the stored next run. Re-enabling a normal cancellation resumes its stored slot; the runner applies its missed-run policy. Manual run-once or an empty recurring slot still calculates a new time."
      ]
    }
  ]
